 "text": "Hello, how are things going? That's annoying. Is it wear on the crank or something else? Lot of them. A few minutes on slow heat and it' be quiet as ghost town. Or you can cut down the wear with a wire brush and then use lot of lube. Set it up on stand so it can't fall over, and heat it in a sink or bath with hot water butty towel between them. Then pull apart a few turns each time before you stop. Straight first, then you see the little dents. About thirty seconds is about all you need. Then dry it totally and oil it with a big hook from your toolbox.",
